            <ArticleTitle>A preliminary examination of over-the-counter medication misuse rates in older adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>187-192</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1551-7411(16)00027-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.sapharm.2016.01.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Older adults are the largest consumers of over the counter (OTC) medications. Of the older adults who are at risk of a major adverse drug event, more than 50% of these events involve an OTC medication.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To explore how older adults select and hypothetically use OTC medications and if the selected medications would be considered safe for use.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Walking interviews were conducted with 20 community-dwelling older adults in a community pharmacy. Each participant selected an OTC medication for a hypothetical pain and sleep scenario. Data were analyzed for four types of misuse: drug-drug interaction, drug-disease interaction, drug-age interaction, and excess usage.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">At least one instance of potential misuse was found in 95% of participants. For sleep medications, drug-drug interactions and drug-age interactions were more common, affecting 50% and 65% of participants respectively. The most common type of misuse noted in the pain products selected was that of drug-drug interaction, with a total of 39 occurrences, affecting 60% of the participants.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">OTC misuse is common among older adults, and it is important for older adults to seek out resources, such as a pharmacist, to help them make safe OTC decisions.</AbstractText>
